        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "0e6fc2f1-5a53-3f6c-a4b4-713d0cc03949",
                "word": "disgrâce",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "08cf388a-6725-4068-b0e8-4951b60022df",
                        "entry_id": "0e6fc2f1-5a53-3f6c-a4b4-713d0cc03949",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "disgrâces"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "300df23e-fc60-38d3-8081-3644133f89a5",
                        "entry_id": "0e6fc2f1-5a53-3f6c-a4b4-713d0cc03949",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Perte, privation des bonnes grâces d’une personne puissante, d’une autorité."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d8b3c17-6f9f-4378-a3e7-3146dfb544e0",
                                "sense_id": "300df23e-fc60-38d3-8081-3644133f89a5",
                                "text": "O mon père, je vous aime et vous vénère, que vous me prodiguiez des trésors de votre bonté, ou les rigueurs de la disgrâce…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0890a29a-d2c5-4188-bbb6-8ff537711ce9",
                                "sense_id": "300df23e-fc60-38d3-8081-3644133f89a5",
                                "text": "Si les cinq ou six complaisants qui témoignaient une amitié si paternelle à Julien eussent déserté l'hôtel de La Mole, la marquise eût été exposée à de grands moments de solitude ; et, aux yeux des femmes de ce rang, la solitude est affreuse : c'est l'emblème de la disgrâce."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e569462c-7b07-34bf-a6f3-744dab26eba6",
                        "entry_id": "0e6fc2f1-5a53-3f6c-a4b4-713d0cc03949",
                        "glosses": [
                            "État de celui que la fortune ne favorise guère."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a6dd19d-9c94-4d56-ba2b-87ed969d9502",
                                "sense_id": "e569462c-7b07-34bf-a6f3-744dab26eba6",
                                "text": "Il lui est survenu une disgrâce. Voilà une étrange, une cruelle disgrâce. Pour comble de disgrâce. Que de disgrâces!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "509c019c-daa6-3e3a-b2de-2485f4c43798",
                        "entry_id": "0e6fc2f1-5a53-3f6c-a4b4-713d0cc03949",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Perte de l'estime, du crédit dont quelqu'un ou quelque chose jouissait auprès de quelqu'un, d'un public."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1d05a84-2df3-41ea-b9e8-5c080161a9d4",
                                "sense_id": "509c019c-daa6-3e3a-b2de-2485f4c43798",
                                "text": "A mon art perverti, mes frasques mondaines et mon endettement notoire s'ajoute à présent la disgrâce, alors que je fais courir le bruit que la crise nerveuse que je traverse est provoquée par le départ inopiné de ma mère. …"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4d53b416-d3c6-3421-8407-4ce54657080a",
                        "entry_id": "0e6fc2f1-5a53-3f6c-a4b4-713d0cc03949",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chute d’une reconnaissance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7bf762ea-a453-453e-909c-f3acbd603e16",
                                "sense_id": "4d53b416-d3c6-3421-8407-4ce54657080a",
                                "text": "Cette plante vient du Mexique, où l’on mange ses racines cuites sous la cendre. Dès le commencement du siècle dernier, on la cultivait en France comme plante alimentaire. Toutefois elle ne tarda pas à être rejetée à cause du goût trop aromatique de ses racines; mais cette disgrâce fît sa fortune, car elle ne disparut de nos potagers que pour entrer dans nos jardins."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "68ba08f3-76ca-4a9d-a545-fc6b94c373f7",
                        "source_entry_id": "0e6fc2f1-5a53-3f6c-a4b4-713d0cc03949",
                        "source_sense_id": "300df23e-fc60-38d3-8081-3644133f89a5",
                        "source_sense_description": "Perte, privation des bonnes grâces d’une personne puissante, d’une autorité.",
                        "target_lang_word": "Ungnade",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Ungnade",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7aea6d10-e34b-3ce0-b378-fa29363b55b6",
                                        "entry_id": "957c4493-d90b-3218-8579-c296e807f5ec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ungunst nach dem Verlust von Beliebtheit oder einer unerwünschten Handlung"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "sprichwörtlich"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b807bc66-90cb-43c0-8008-b63f384ba245",
                                                "sense_id": "7aea6d10-e34b-3ce0-b378-fa29363b55b6",
                                                "text": "„Seine krawalligen Methoden haben ihn einst bereits in Ungnade stürzen lassen. Wer ist der Mann?“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57413508-30d7-4d32-887c-90286e9129b3",
                                                "sense_id": "7aea6d10-e34b-3ce0-b378-fa29363b55b6",
                                                "text": "„Die Gemahlin König Philipps V., die aus Parma stammte, hatte Intrigen gesponnen, die Brischi nötigten, den Hof zu verlassen, nachdem der Marqués de la Enseneda in Ungnade gefallen war.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55cb57cb-efb9-489d-8425-bfa87adcb423",
                                                "sense_id": "7aea6d10-e34b-3ce0-b378-fa29363b55b6",
                                                "text": "„Gerüchte, Gründgens sei in Ungnade gefallen, vielleicht sogar im KZ gelandet, dringen auch nach außen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0abaf843-9fa8-498d-aec8-11edcc119b2a",
                        "source_entry_id": "0e6fc2f1-5a53-3f6c-a4b4-713d0cc03949",
                        "source_sense_id": "300df23e-fc60-38d3-8081-3644133f89a5",
                        "source_sense_description": "Perte, privation des bonnes grâces d’une personne puissante, d’une autorité.",
                        "target_lang_word": "disgrace",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "disgrace",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af9f5d1c-214c-3f41-8c98-ba33b4a6b5be",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of being out of favor; loss of favor, regard, or respect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbc174b0-9d1e-4575-ac38-d9b3727b12c9",
                                                "sense_id": "af9f5d1c-214c-3f41-8c98-ba33b4a6b5be",
                                                "text": "I heare / Macduffe liues in diſgrace. Sir, can you tell / Where he beſtowes himſelfe?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6be99cd5-8000-39e5-aab9-78c3cfd109e1",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being dishonored, or covered with shame."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7756053a-8f4a-47b8-a6dc-35ce986c9d1f",
                                                "sense_id": "6be99cd5-8000-39e5-aab9-78c3cfd109e1",
                                                "text": "Now she lives in disgrace."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "161ed4fb-fdb4-3973-bd91-75d3def376ac",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something which brings dishonor; the cause of reproach or shame; great discredit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6366a8e0-9952-49d6-826e-46e7372d03ac",
                                                "sense_id": "161ed4fb-fdb4-3973-bd91-75d3def376ac",
                                                "text": "His behaviour at the party was a total disgrace! He was leeching on all the ladies, and insulting the men."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0e8ca50-9b33-4a8d-8471-0825a5e950d1",
                                                "sense_id": "161ed4fb-fdb4-3973-bd91-75d3def376ac",
                                                "text": "Practice and whipping were alike unavailing, and Epps, satisfied of it at last, swore I was a disgrace—that I was not fit to associate with a cotton-picking \"nigger\"—that I could not pick enough in a day to pay the trouble of weighing it, and that I should go into the cotton field no more."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74fcdf24-767f-3906-890a-83d77428e0ad",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act of unkindness; a disfavor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "358e13b3-720c-4406-b42c-04b97bbfb423",
                                                "sense_id": "74fcdf24-767f-3906-890a-83d77428e0ad",
                                                "text": "As for the pulling of them [ambitious men] downe, if the Affaires require it, and that it may not be done with ſafety ſuddainly, the onely Way is, the Enterchange, continually of Fauours, and Diſgraces, whereby they may not know, what to expect; And be, as it were, in a Wood."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "disgrace",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e20ef1d8-7040-3dc1-b0a5-da0a9fb4735f",
                                        "entry_id": "3de008e8-961c-3a15-a0c5-566717b3bb8c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put someone or something out of favor; to bring shame or ignominy upon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e07fe5c7-a9db-4a30-a640-26c42383455e",
                                                "sense_id": "e20ef1d8-7040-3dc1-b0a5-da0a9fb4735f",
                                                "text": "[…] some families renounced the use of a certain praenomen which had been disgraced by one of their name […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
